---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { rel, SUPPORT_EMAIL, LEGAL_NAME } from '../../consts';
const description = `Privacy policy for Last Human: Dodge the Bots by ${LEGAL_NAME}.`;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy · Last Human: Dodge the Bots" description={description} path="/privacy/last-human">
  <main class="page">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:720px;">
      <a class="back" href={rel('/privacy/')}>← All privacy policies</a>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last Human: Dodge the Bots · Effective date: September 5, 2026</p>

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        {LEGAL_NAME} operates Last Human, a free arcade game supported by ads. There are no accounts, and
        we never see your high score or app settings — those stay on your device. Last Human sends
        <strong>anonymous crash reports</strong> (Sentry) and, unless you turn it off in Settings,
        <strong>anonymous usage analytics</strong> (PostHog) — both described below. Neither is linked to
        your identity or used to track you, and neither is used for advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your persistent high score.</li>
        <li>Your app settings, including purchase/ads state.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        This information is stored locally on your device. We do not receive it. Deleting the app removes
        local app data from your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Usage analytics (PostHog) — on by default, with a Settings opt-out</h2>
      <p>
        Last Human sends a small set of anonymous, bucketed product events — for example, that a level was
        started or completed, how many attempts it took, or that Remove Ads was purchased — never your
        score, your progress, or anything you type. Events are tied to a random ID generated on your
        device, not to your name or any account (Last Human has no accounts). Analytics is on by default;
        you can turn it off any time in <strong>Settings → Privacy</strong>.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Turning analytics off stops new events immediately, clears the send queue on your device, and resets your ID.</li>
        <li>Events already sent are kept for <strong>90 days</strong> as individual records and up to <strong>13 months</strong> as aggregated statistics.</li>
        <li>To have your already-sent events deleted, copy the analytics ID shown under the toggle in Settings and email it to <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a> — copy it before turning analytics off, since switching off resets the ID.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Crash reporting (Sentry) — always on</h2>
      <p>
        If Last Human crashes, it sends an anonymous crash report — the stack trace and your iOS version —
        so we can find and fix the problem. A crash report never contains your score, your progress, or
        anything else you typed or saved. There is no switch for crash reporting, because a report carries
        no user data to begin with. Crash reports are kept for <strong>30 days</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising (Google AdMob)</h2>
      <p>
        The free version may show an interstitial ad every few levels — never mid-level. Ads are served by
        <strong>Google AdMob</strong>, a third-party advertising network. Last Human requests
        <strong>non-personalized</strong> ads and does not show Apple's tracking prompt, because it does
        not ask for cross-app tracking. Last Human does not show ads at all to players in the EU, EEA, or
        UK. To serve and measure ads, Google may still collect device information such as a device
        identifier, IP address, and coarse ad-interaction data. We do not receive, store, or link any of
        this to you, and it is never joined with the analytics described above.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>How Google uses this data is described in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads">Google's advertising policy</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google's privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li>The optional Remove Ads purchase ($0.99) removes ads from the app.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Used to track you</h2>
      <p>
        None of the data described on this page is used to track you across other companies' apps or
        websites, and none of it is combined with data from a data broker. This is true for analytics,
        crash reports, and advertising alike.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        We do not knowingly collect any data from anyone, including children under 13. There are no
        accounts, profiles, or in-app messaging.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy ever changes materially, the new version will be posted at this URL with an updated
        date above. Continued use of the app after a change constitutes acceptance.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions? Email <a href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
